We have a task: build complete route of chemicals based on inputs. We have template search gave mapped_rxn and template_id 1914386. Apply_template gave precursors list: ['C#C[Si](C)(C)C', 'COC(=O)C(=O)CCc1ccccc1'].

We verified step is valid, and both precursors are buyable.

Now need to construct JSON route: root molecule is target. What is target SMILES? The target is the product of the step. The mapped_rxn shows product: [CH:14]#[C:15][Si:16]([CH3:17])([CH3:18])[CH3:19].O=[C:5]([C:3]([O:2][CH3:1])=[O:4])[CH2:6][CH2:7][c:8]1[cH:9][cH:10][cH:11][cH:12][cH:13]1>>[CH3:1][O:2][C:3](=[O:4])[C:5]1(/[CH:6]=[CH:7]/[c:8]2[cH:9][cH:10][cH:11][cH:12][cH:13]2)[CH:14]=[C:15]1[Si:16]([CH3:17])([CH3:18])[CH3:19]

Thus product SMILES is the right side: [CH3:1][O:2][C:3](=[O:4])[C:5]1(/[CH:6]=[CH:7]/[c:8]2[cH:9][cH:10][cH:11][cH:12][cH:13]2)[CH:14]=[C:15]1[Si:16]([CH3:17])([CH3:18])[CH3:19]

We need to convert to canonical SMILES without atom mapping. The earlier verification used "COC(=O)C1(/C=C/c2ccccc2)C=C1[Si](C)(C)C". That seems to be the product SMILES. Let's confirm: The product is a silyl-substituted cyclohexene with phenyl? Actually the product includes aromatic ring fused? The SMILES they used: COC(=O)C1(/C=C/c2ccccc2)C=C1[Si](C)(C)C. That matches the product: methyl ester? Wait COC(=O) is methyl ester of something. The product includes a phenyl attached to a double bond. So target SMILES is "COC(=O)C1(/C=C/c2ccccc2)C=C1[Si](C)(C)C". We'll use that.

Now construct route JSON:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"COC(=O)C1(/C=C/c2ccccc2)C=C1[Si](C)(C)C",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":1914386,
     "children":[
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"C#C[Si](C)(C)C"},
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"COC(=O)C(=O)CCc1ccccc1"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

Check schema: reaction must have at least two children. Good.

Now we should verify route schema using verify_route tool.
